cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its outputs, please cite the associated preprint below."
title: "A comparative assessment of global building and settlement datasets across geographic and settlement contexts"
abstract: >-
  Global building and settlement products increasingly support population
  mapping, exposure assessment, and urban monitoring, yet comparative evidence
  remains fragmented across representations, geographic contexts, and
  evaluation methods. This software implements a representation-aware framework
  for benchmarking seven global or near-global products against harmonized
  reference building footprints across 135 study areas.
